  · drop  [DMA address semantics and validation] net/smc/smc_loopback.c:21

  SMC_DMA_ADDR_INVALID as ~(dma_addr_t)0 may not be portable. The constant ~(dma_addr_t)0 is used to indicate an invalid DMA address for loopback-ism where no real DMA mapping exists. While this works on architectures where dma_addr_t is 32 or 64 bits,
